  "notes": "{傷|きず}つける means to hurt, injure, or wound—either physically or emotionally.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- {傷|きず}つける (transitive): to hurt, wound\n- {傷|きず}つく (intransitive): to get hurt, be wounded\n\nCONJUGATION (ichidan):\n- {傷|きず}つけない (negative)\n- {傷|きず}つけます (polite)\n- {傷|きず}つけた (past)\n- {傷|きず}つけて (te-form)\n- {傷|きず}つけられる (passive: to be hurt)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {人|ひと}を{傷|きず}つける: to hurt someone\n- {心|こころ}を{傷|きず}つける: to hurt someone's feelings\n- {体|からだ}を{傷|きず}つける: to injure one's body\n- {車|くるま}を{傷|きず}つける: to scratch a car\n- {傷|きず}つけるつもりはなかった: I didn't mean to hurt you\n\nWORD FORMATION:\n{傷|きず} (wound) + つける (attach/cause) = to cause a wound\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {傷|きず}: wound, injury, scratch\n- {傷|きず}つきやすい: easily hurt, sensitive\n- {怪我|けが}をさせる: to injure (cause injury)",
